# Ignore rules for apps/playground/Dockerfile.
#
# The name matters. This image builds with the REPO ROOT as context, and Docker
# looks for the ignore file at the CONTEXT root — so a file at
# apps/playground/.dockerignore is silently never read, and the whole monorepo
# (every node_modules) gets sent to the daemon. BuildKit also honours
# "<dockerfile>.dockerignore", which is this file: it stays next to the
# Dockerfile it belongs to without imposing rules on other builds from the root.
#
# Patterns are context-relative, i.e. relative to the repo root.

**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/build

# Rendered demos — hundreds of MB of local scratch, never part of an image.
apps/playground/output

# Secrets must arrive via BuildKit secrets or runtime env, never a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

.git
.github
.vscode
.claude
**/*.log
**/coverage
